IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `wra-core`
IMPORT `wra4-ss96-97`
IMPORT `wra4-ss127-129`

-- Welfare Reform Act 2012 (United Kingdom), 2012 c. 5, Part 5, ss 130 to 134: sharing information with and between local
-- authorities (s 130 overnight care, s 131 welfare services and council tax), the offence of unlawful disclosure (s 132),
-- supplementary provision (s 133) and amendments (s 134). Layer 1, part wra4. Host Act named in labels: none (these sections
-- stand on their own). Acts named in the text: SSAA (Social Security Administration Act 1992).
-- A "may" is a power the text grants (JUST TRUE where the facts fit it, NOTHING where they do not, because nothing here says
-- the information may not be shared otherwise). Result convention: JUST FALSE / FALSE = the text says no; NOTHING = not
-- covered (see wra4-ss96-97.l4).

§ `s 130 -- information-sharing in relation to the provision of overnight care`

-- 130(3): "relevant service" means (a) overnight care in the individual's own home provided by or on behalf of a local
-- authority, (b) a residential care service provided by or on behalf of a local authority, (c) overnight hospital accommodation.
DECLARE `s 130(3) kind of service` IS ONE OF
    `s 130(3)(a) a service consisting of overnight care in the individual's own home provided by or on behalf of a local authority`
    `s 130(3)(b) a residential care service provided by or on behalf of a local authority`
    `s 130(3)(c) a service consisting of overnight hospital accommodation`
    `s 130(3) some other service`

-- src:2339 | (3) In this section “relevant service means—
-- src:2340 | (a) a service consisting of overnight care in the individual's own home provided by or on behalf of a local authority;
-- src:2341 | (b) a residential care service provided by or on behalf of a local authority;
-- src:2342 | (c) a service consisting of overnight hospital accommodation.
@ref s 130(3) (src:2339-2342)
GIVEN `the service` IS A `s 130(3) kind of service`  @desc What kind of service is it?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 130(3) the service is a relevant service` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the service`
    WHEN `s 130(3)(a) a service consisting of overnight care in the individual's own home provided by or on behalf of a local authority` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `s 130(3)(b) a residential care service provided by or on behalf of a local authority` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `s 130(3)(c) a service consisting of overnight hospital accommodation` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `s 130(3) some other service` THEN FALSE         -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "“relevant service means— (a) ... (b) ... (c) ..."

-- 130(4): "hospital accommodation" means, in England, accommodation within the meaning of the NHS Act 2006 provided by an NHS trust
-- or an NHS foundation trust; in Wales, within the meaning of the NHS (Wales) Act 2006 provided by a Local Health Board or an
-- NHS trust; in Scotland, within the meaning of the NHS (Scotland) Act 1978 provided by a Health Board or Special Health Board
-- but excluding accommodation in an institution for dental treatment maintained in connection with a dental school.
DECLARE `s 130(4) provider of the accommodation` IS ONE OF
    `s 130(4) an NHS trust`
    `s 130(4) an NHS foundation trust`
    `s 130(4) a Local Health Board`
    `s 130(4) a Health Board or Special Health Board`
    `s 130(4) some other provider`

-- src:2343 | (4) In subsection (3)(c) “hospital accommodation” means—
-- src:2344 | (a) in relation to England, hospital accommodation within the meaning of the National Health Service Act 2006 which is provided by ... an NHS trust or an NHS foundation trust;
-- src:2345 | (b) in relation to Wales, hospital accommodation within the meaning of the National Health Service (Wales) Act 2006 which is provided by a Local Health Board or an NHS trust;
-- src:2346 | (c) in relation to Scotland, hospital accommodation within the meaning of the National Health Service (Scotland) Act 1978 which is provided by a Health Board or Special Health Board but excluding accommodation in an institution for providing dental treatment maintained in connection with a dental school.
@ref s 130(4) (src:2343-2346)
GIVEN `the place` IS A Place  @desc In which country is the accommodation?
      `the accommodation is hospital accommodation within the meaning of the National Health Service Act for that country` IS A BOOLEAN  @desc Is it hospital accommodation within the meaning of the National Health Service Act that applies to that country?
      `the provider` IS A `s 130(4) provider of the accommodation`  @desc Who provides the accommodation?
      `the accommodation is in an institution for providing dental treatment maintained in connection with a dental school` IS A BOOLEAN  @desc Is the accommodation in an institution for providing dental treatment maintained in connection with a dental school?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 130(4) the accommodation is hospital accommodation` MEANS
    IF (NOT (`the accommodation is hospital accommodation within the meaning of the National Health Service Act for that country`))
    THEN FALSE                                            -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "hospital accommodation within the meaning of the National Health Service ... Act"
    ELSE (CONSIDER `the place`
          WHEN `Greater London` THEN (`the provider` EQUALS `s 130(4) an NHS trust`) OR (`the provider` EQUALS `s 130(4) an NHS foundation trust`)          -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words) where false: "(a) in relation to England, ... provided by ... an NHS trust or an NHS foundation trust"
          WHEN `England outside Greater London` THEN (`the provider` EQUALS `s 130(4) an NHS trust`) OR (`the provider` EQUALS `s 130(4) an NHS foundation trust`)   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words) where false: "(a) in relation to England, ... provided by ... an NHS trust or an NHS foundation trust"
          WHEN Wales THEN (`the provider` EQUALS `s 130(4) a Local Health Board`) OR (`the provider` EQUALS `s 130(4) an NHS trust`)                                 -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words) where false: "(b) in relation to Wales, ... provided by a Local Health Board or an NHS trust"
          WHEN Scotland THEN (`the provider` EQUALS `s 130(4) a Health Board or Special Health Board`) AND (NOT (`the accommodation is in an institution for providing dental treatment maintained in connection with a dental school`))   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words) where false: "(c) in relation to Scotland, ... provided by a Health Board or Special Health Board but excluding accommodation in an institution for providing dental treatment maintained in connection with a dental school"
          WHEN `Northern Ireland` THEN FALSE              -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): the definition has a paragraph for England, Wales and Scotland only
          WHEN `outside the United Kingdom` THEN FALSE)   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): the definition has a paragraph for England, Wales and Scotland only

-- 130(2): the information is (a) the fact of the provision or likely provision of the service, (b) when it begins or ends or is
-- likely to, (c) other prescribed information relating to the service and how it is funded.
DECLARE `s 130(2) kind of information` IS ONE OF
    `s 130(2)(a) information as to the fact of the provision or likely provision of the service`
    `s 130(2)(b) information about when the provision of the service begins or ends or is likely to do so`
    `s 130(2)(c) other information relating to the service provided and how it is funded`
    `s 130(2) some other information`

-- src:2335 | (2) The information referred to in subsection (1) is—
-- src:2336 | (a) information as to the fact of the provision or likely provision of the service;
-- src:2337 | (b) information about when the provision of the service begins or ends or is likely to do so;
-- src:2338 | (c) other prescribed information relating to the service provided and how it is funded (including the extent to which it is funded by the recipient).
@ref s 130(2) (src:2335-2338)
GIVEN `the information` IS A `s 130(2) kind of information`  @desc What is the information about?
      `the information is prescribed` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN  @desc Do regulations prescribe the information? Leave out if not known.
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 130(2) the information falls within subsection (2)` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the information`
    WHEN `s 130(2)(a) information as to the fact of the provision or likely provision of the service` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 130(2)(b) information about when the provision of the service begins or ends or is likely to do so` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 130(2)(c) other information relating to the service provided and how it is funded` THEN
        CONSIDER `the information is prescribed`
        WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING                         -- NOTHING-kind (undefined term): "other prescribed information" is whatever regulations prescribe
        WHEN JUST prescribed THEN JUST prescribed         -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words) where false: "(c) other prescribed information relating to the service provided and how it is funded"
    WHEN `s 130(2) some other information` THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The information referred to in subsection (1) is— (a) ... (b) ... (c) ..."

-- 130(1): the section applies where a local authority holds information within (2) in relation to a person who is receiving or is
-- likely to receive a relevant service.
-- src:2334 | (1) This section applies where a local authority holds information falling within subsection (2) in relation to a person who is receiving or is likely to receive a relevant service.
@ref s 130(1) (src:2334-2334)
GIVEN `a local authority holds the information` IS A BOOLEAN  @desc Does a local authority hold the information?
      `the information falls within subsection (2)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN  @desc Is it information as to the fact, timing or funding of the service? Leave out if not known.
      `the person is receiving or is likely to receive a relevant service` IS A BOOLEAN  @desc Are you receiving, or likely to receive, overnight care at home, a residential care service or overnight hospital accommodation?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 130(1) this section applies` MEANS
    IF `a local authority holds the information`
       AND (`the information falls within subsection (2)` EQUALS JUST TRUE)
       AND `the person is receiving or is likely to receive a relevant service`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING                                          -- NOTHING-kind (limited by own wording): "This section applies where ..."; the subsection does not say it applies only then

-- 130(7): "relevant benefit" means (a) universal credit, (b) housing benefit, (c) council tax benefit, (d) any prescribed benefit.
-- src:2356 | (7) In this section “relevant benefit“ means—
-- src:2357 | (a) universal credit;
-- src:2358 | (b) housing benefit;
-- src:2359 | (c) council tax benefit;
-- src:2360 | (d) any prescribed benefit.
@ref s 130(7) (src:2356-2360)
GIVEN `the benefit` IS A Benefit  @desc Which benefit is in question?
      `regulations prescribe the benefit` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN  @desc Do regulations prescribe the benefit as a relevant benefit? Leave out if not known.
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 130(7) the benefit is a relevant benefit` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the benefit`
    WHEN `universal credit` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `housing benefit` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `council tax benefit` THEN JUST TRUE
    OTHERWISE
        CONSIDER `regulations prescribe the benefit`
        WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING                         -- NOTHING-kind (undefined term): "any prescribed benefit" is whatever regulations prescribe
        WHEN JUST prescribed THEN JUST prescribed         -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words) where false: "“relevant benefit“ means— (a) ...; (b) ...; (c) ...; (d) any prescribed benefit"

-- 130(6): the persons to whom the information may be supplied under (5)(b): (a) the Secretary of State, (b) a person providing
-- services to the Secretary of State, (c) a local authority, (d) a person authorised to exercise a local authority function
-- relating to a relevant benefit, (e) a person providing services relating to a relevant benefit to a local authority.
DECLARE `s 130(6) person` IS ONE OF
    `s 130(6)(a) the Secretary of State`
    `s 130(6)(b) a person providing services to the Secretary of State`
    `s 130(6)(c) a local authority`
    `s 130(6)(d) a person authorised to exercise any function of a local authority relating to a relevant benefit`
    `s 130(6)(e) a person providing services relating to a relevant benefit to a local authority`
    `s 130(6) some other person`

-- src:2350 | (6) The persons referred to in subsection (5) are—
-- src:2351 | (a) the Secretary of State;
-- src:2352 | (b) a person providing services to the Secretary of State;
-- src:2353 | (c) a local authority;
-- src:2354 | (d) a person authorised to exercise any function of a local authority relating to a relevant benefit;
-- src:2355 | (e) a person providing services relating to a relevant benefit to a local authority.
@ref s 130(6) (src:2350-2355)
GIVEN `the person` IS A `s 130(6) person`  @desc Who would the information be supplied to?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 130(6) the person is a person specified in subsection (6)` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the person`
    WHEN `s 130(6)(a) the Secretary of State` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `s 130(6)(b) a person providing services to the Secretary of State` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `s 130(6)(c) a local authority` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `s 130(6)(d) a person authorised to exercise any function of a local authority relating to a relevant benefit` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `s 130(6)(e) a person providing services relating to a relevant benefit to a local authority` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `s 130(6) some other person` THEN FALSE          -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The persons referred to in subsection (5) are— (a) ... (e) ..."

-- 130(5): the local authority may (a) itself use the information for purposes relating to the payment of a relevant benefit to
-- the individual, or (b) supply it to a person in (6) for those purposes.
DECLARE `s 130(5) what the local authority does` IS ONE OF
    `s 130(5)(a) itself uses the information`
    `s 130(5)(b) supplies the information to another person`
    `s 130(5) does something else with the information`

-- src:2347 | (5) The local authority may—
-- src:2348 | (a) itself use the information for purposes relating to the payment of a relevant benefit to the individual, or
-- src:2349 | (b) supply the information to a person specified in subsection (6) for those purposes.
@ref s 130(5) (src:2347-2349)
GIVEN `this section applies` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN  @desc Does section 130 apply to the information? Leave out if not known.
      `what the local authority does` IS A `s 130(5) what the local authority does`  @desc What would the local authority do with the information?
      `the purposes relate to the payment of a relevant benefit to the individual` IS A BOOLEAN  @desc Are the purposes ones relating to the payment of a relevant benefit to you?
      `the recipient is a person specified in subsection (6)` IS A BOOLEAN  @desc Is the person to be given the information one of those listed in section 130(6)?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 130(5) the local authority may use or supply the information` MEANS
    IF (`this section applies` EQUALS JUST TRUE) AND `the purposes relate to the payment of a relevant benefit to the individual`
       AND (CONSIDER `what the local authority does`
            WHEN `s 130(5)(a) itself uses the information` THEN TRUE
            WHEN `s 130(5)(b) supplies the information to another person` THEN `the recipient is a person specified in subsection (6)`
            WHEN `s 130(5) does something else with the information` THEN FALSE)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING                                          -- NOTHING-kind (limited by own wording): "The local authority may (a) ... or (b) ..."; the subsection says nothing of other use or supply

-- 130(8): regulations under (7)(d) may not prescribe a benefit provision for which is within the legislative competence of the
-- Scottish Parliament.
-- src:2361 | (8) Regulations under subsection (7)(d) may not prescribe a benefit provision for which is within the legislative competence of the Scottish Parliament.
@ref s 130(8) (src:2361-2361)
GIVEN `provision for the benefit is within the legislative competence of the Scottish Parliament` IS A BOOLEAN  @desc Is provision for the benefit within the legislative competence of the Scottish Parliament?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 130(8) regulations may prescribe the benefit` MEANS
    IF `provision for the benefit is within the legislative competence of the Scottish Parliament`
    THEN JUST FALSE                                       -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Regulations under subsection (7)(d) may not prescribe a benefit provision for which is within the legislative competence of the Scottish Parliament"
    ELSE NOTHING                                          -- NOTHING-kind (limited by own wording): the subsection bars one class of benefit; for any other it says nothing

§ `s 131 -- information-sharing in relation to welfare services and council tax`

-- 131(11): "qualifying person" means (a) a local authority, (b) a person authorised to exercise a function of such an authority
-- relating to welfare services or council tax, (c) a person providing services to a local authority relating to welfare
-- services or council tax, (d) an authority which administers housing benefit, (e) a person authorised to exercise a function of
-- such an authority relating to housing benefit, (f) a person providing such an authority services relating to housing benefit,
-- (g) a person prescribed or of a description prescribed by the Secretary of State.
DECLARE `s 131(11) description of person` IS ONE OF
    `s 131(11)(a) a local authority`
    `s 131(11)(b) a person authorised to exercise any function of a local authority relating to welfare services or council tax`
    `s 131(11)(c) a person providing services to a local authority relating to welfare services or council tax`
    `s 131(11)(d) an authority which administers housing benefit`
    `s 131(11)(e) a person authorised to exercise any function of an authority which administers housing benefit relating to housing benefit`
    `s 131(11)(f) a person providing to an authority which administers housing benefit services relating to housing benefit`
    `s 131(11)(g) a person prescribed or of a description prescribed by the Secretary of State`
    `s 131(11) some other person`

-- src:2391 | (11) In this section “qualifying person“ means—
-- src:2392 | (a) a local authority;
-- src:2393 | (b) a person authorised to exercise any function of such an authority relating to welfare services or council tax;
-- src:2394 | (c) a person providing services to a local authority relating to welfare services or council tax;
-- src:2395 | (d) an authority which administers housing benefit;
-- src:2396 | (e) a person authorised to exercise any function of such an authority relating to housing benefit;
-- src:2397 | (f) a person providing to such an authority services relating to housing benefit; or
-- src:2398 | (g) a person prescribed or of a description prescribed by the Secretary of State.
@ref s 131(11) (src:2391-2398)
GIVEN `the person` IS A `s 131(11) description of person`  @desc Which description fits the person?
      `the Secretary of State prescribes the person` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN  @desc Does the Secretary of State prescribe the person, or a description that fits them, as a qualifying person? Leave out if not known.
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 131(11) the person is a qualifying person` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the person`
    WHEN `s 131(11)(a) a local authority` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 131(11)(b) a person authorised to exercise any function of a local authority relating to welfare services or council tax` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 131(11)(c) a person providing services to a local authority relating to welfare services or council tax` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 131(11)(d) an authority which administers housing benefit` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 131(11)(e) a person authorised to exercise any function of an authority which administers housing benefit relating to housing benefit` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 131(11)(f) a person providing to an authority which administers housing benefit services relating to housing benefit` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 131(11)(g) a person prescribed or of a description prescribed by the Secretary of State` THEN
        CONSIDER `the Secretary of State prescribes the person`
        WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING                         -- NOTHING-kind (undefined term): who is prescribed is whatever the Secretary of State prescribes
        WHEN JUST prescribed THEN JUST prescribed         -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words) where false: "(g) a person prescribed or of a description prescribed by the Secretary of State"
    WHEN `s 131(11) some other person` THEN JUST FALSE    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "“qualifying person“ means— (a) ... (g) ..."

-- 131(1): the Secretary of State, or a person providing services to the Secretary of State, may supply relevant information to a
-- qualifying person for prescribed purposes relating to welfare services or council tax.
-- src:2363 | (1) The Secretary of State, or a person providing services to the Secretary of State, may supply relevant information to a qualifying person for prescribed purposes relating to welfare services or council tax.
@ref s 131(1) (src:2363-2363)
GIVEN `the supplier is the Secretary of State or a person providing services to the Secretary of State` IS A BOOLEAN  @desc Is the supplier the Secretary of State, or a person providing services to the Secretary of State?
      `the information is relevant information` IS A BOOLEAN  @desc Is the information about a relevant social security benefit or about welfare services?
      `the recipient is a qualifying person` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN  @desc Is the recipient a qualifying person? Leave out if not known.
      `the purpose is a prescribed purpose relating to welfare services or council tax` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN  @desc Is the purpose one regulations prescribe for welfare services or council tax? Leave out if not known.
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 131(1) the Secretary of State may supply the information to a qualifying person` MEANS
    IF `the supplier is the Secretary of State or a person providing services to the Secretary of State` AND `the information is relevant information`
       AND (`the recipient is a qualifying person` EQUALS JUST TRUE) AND (`the purpose is a prescribed purpose relating to welfare services or council tax` EQUALS JUST TRUE)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING                                          -- NOTHING-kind (limited by own wording): "may supply" to a qualifying person for prescribed purposes; nothing says it may not be supplied otherwise

-- 131(2): a qualifying person who holds relevant information for a prescribed purpose relating to welfare services may supply
-- it to (a) the Secretary of State or (b) a person providing services to the Secretary of State, for a prescribed purpose
-- relating to a relevant social security benefit.
-- src:2364 | (2) A qualifying person who holds relevant information for a prescribed purpose relating to welfare services may supply that information to—
-- src:2365 | (a) the Secretary of State, or
-- src:2366 | (b) a person providing services to the Secretary of State,
-- src:2367 | for a prescribed purpose relating to a relevant social security benefit.
@ref s 131(2) (src:2364-2367)
GIVEN `the holder is a qualifying person` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN  @desc Is the holder a qualifying person? Leave out if not known.
      `the information is relevant information held for a prescribed purpose relating to welfare services` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN  @desc Is it relevant information the holder holds for a prescribed purpose relating to welfare services? Leave out if not known.
      `the recipient is the Secretary of State or a person providing services to the Secretary of State` IS A BOOLEAN  @desc Is the recipient the Secretary of State, or a person providing services to the Secretary of State?
      `the purpose is a prescribed purpose relating to a relevant social security benefit` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN  @desc Is the purpose one regulations prescribe for a relevant social security benefit? Leave out if not known.
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 131(2) the qualifying person may supply the information to the Secretary of State` MEANS
    IF (`the holder is a qualifying person` EQUALS JUST TRUE)
       AND (`the information is relevant information held for a prescribed purpose relating to welfare services` EQUALS JUST TRUE)
       AND `the recipient is the Secretary of State or a person providing services to the Secretary of State`
       AND (`the purpose is a prescribed purpose relating to a relevant social security benefit` EQUALS JUST TRUE)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING                                          -- NOTHING-kind (limited by own wording): "may supply that information to" these recipients for this purpose; nothing says it may not be supplied otherwise

-- 131(3): a qualifying person who holds relevant information for a prescribed purpose relating to welfare services, council tax
-- or housing benefit may (a) use it for another such prescribed purpose, or (b) supply it to another qualifying person for use
-- in relation to the same or another such prescribed purpose.
-- src:2368 | (3) A qualifying person who holds relevant information for a prescribed purpose relating to welfare services, council tax or housing benefit may—
-- src:2369 | (a) use the information for another prescribed purpose relating to welfare services, council tax or housing benefit;
-- src:2370 | (b) supply it to another qualifying person for use in relation to the same or another prescribed purpose relating to welfare services, council tax or housing benefit.
@ref s 131(3) (src:2368-2370)
GIVEN `the holder is a qualifying person` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN  @desc Is the holder a qualifying person? Leave out if not known.
      `the information is relevant information held for a prescribed purpose relating to welfare services, council tax or housing benefit` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN  @desc Is it relevant information the holder holds for a prescribed purpose relating to welfare services, council tax or housing benefit? Leave out if not known.
      `the holder uses it for another prescribed purpose of that kind` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN  @desc Would the holder use it for another prescribed purpose of that kind? Leave out if not known.
      `the holder supplies it to another qualifying person for use for a prescribed purpose of that kind` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN  @desc Would the holder supply it to another qualifying person for use for a prescribed purpose of that kind? Leave out if not known.
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 131(3) the qualifying person may use or supply the information` MEANS
    IF (`the holder is a qualifying person` EQUALS JUST TRUE)
       AND (`the information is relevant information held for a prescribed purpose relating to welfare services, council tax or housing benefit` EQUALS JUST TRUE)
       AND ((`the holder uses it for another prescribed purpose of that kind` EQUALS JUST TRUE) OR (`the holder supplies it to another qualifying person for use for a prescribed purpose of that kind` EQUALS JUST TRUE))
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING                                          -- NOTHING-kind (limited by own wording): "may (a) use ... (b) supply ..."; nothing says it may not be used or supplied otherwise

-- 131(4) and (5): relevant information supplied under (1) or (3) to a qualifying person may be supplied by that person to a person
-- who provides qualifying welfare services for purposes connected with those services; services are qualifying welfare services
-- if (a) a local authority, or (b) a person who is a qualifying person by virtue of (11)(g), contributes or will contribute to
-- the expenditure incurred in their provision.
-- src:2372 | (5) In subsection (4) services are qualifying welfare services if—
-- src:2373 | (a) a local authority, or
-- src:2374 | (b) a person who is a qualifying person by virtue of subsection (11) (g),
-- src:2375 | contributes or will contribute to the expenditure incurred in their provision.
@ref s 131(5) (src:2372-2375)
GIVEN `a local authority contributes or will contribute to the expenditure incurred in the provision of the services` IS A BOOLEAN  @desc Does a local authority contribute, or will it contribute, to the expenditure on the services?
      `a person who is a qualifying person by virtue of subsection (11)(g) contributes or will contribute to that expenditure` IS A BOOLEAN  @desc Does a person prescribed as a qualifying person contribute, or will they contribute, to that expenditure?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 131(5) the services are qualifying welfare services` MEANS
    IF `a local authority contributes or will contribute to the expenditure incurred in the provision of the services`
       OR `a person who is a qualifying person by virtue of subsection (11)(g) contributes or will contribute to that expenditure`
    THEN TRUE
    ELSE FALSE                                            -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "services are qualifying welfare services if (a) a local authority, or (b) a person who is a qualifying person by virtue of subsection (11)(g), contributes or will contribute to the expenditure"

-- src:2371 | (4) Relevant information supplied under subsection (1) or (3) to a qualifying person may be supplied by that person to a person who provides qualifying welfare services for purposes connected with the provision of those services.
@ref s 131(4) (src:2371-2371)
GIVEN `the information was supplied under subsection (1) or (3) to a qualifying person` IS A BOOLEAN  @desc Was the information supplied to the holder under section 131(1) or (3)?
      `the information is relevant information` IS A BOOLEAN  @desc Is the information about a relevant social security benefit or about welfare services?
      `the recipient provides qualifying welfare services` IS A BOOLEAN  @desc Does the recipient provide qualifying welfare services?
      `the purposes are connected with the provision of those services` IS A BOOLEAN  @desc Are the purposes connected with the provision of those services?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 131(4) the qualifying person may supply the information to a person who provides qualifying welfare services` MEANS
    IF `the information was supplied under subsection (1) or (3) to a qualifying person` AND `the information is relevant information`
       AND `the recipient provides qualifying welfare services` AND `the purposes are connected with the provision of those services`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING                                          -- NOTHING-kind (limited by own wording): "may be supplied by that person to a person who provides qualifying welfare services for purposes connected with"; nothing says it may not be supplied otherwise

-- 131(7), (9): "excepted information" is information held by the Welsh (Scottish) body that (i) is not supplied by, or derived from
-- information supplied to another person by, the Secretary of State or a person providing services to the Secretary of State or
-- a person engaged in the administration of housing benefit, and (ii) is held only for an excepted purpose. 131(7)(b), (9)(b):
-- an excepted purpose relates to a matter provision for which is within the legislative competence of the National Assembly for
-- Wales or made by the Welsh Ministers (Scottish Parliament).
-- src:2378 | (a) excepted information is information held by the Welsh body that—
-- src:2379 | (i) is not supplied by, or derived from information supplied to another person by, the Secretary of State or a person providing services to the Secretary of State or a person engaged in the administration of housing benefit, and
-- src:2380 | (ii) is held only for an excepted purpose;
@ref s 131(7)(a) (src:2378-2380)
GIVEN `the information is supplied by, or derived from information supplied to another person by, the Secretary of State or a person providing services to the Secretary of State or a person engaged in the administration of housing benefit` IS A BOOLEAN  @desc Was the information supplied by, or derived from information supplied by, the Secretary of State, a person providing services to the Secretary of State or a person who administers housing benefit?
      `the information is held only for an excepted purpose` IS A BOOLEAN  @desc Is the information held only for an excepted purpose?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 131(7)(a) the information held by the Welsh body is excepted information` MEANS
    IF (NOT (`the information is supplied by, or derived from information supplied to another person by, the Secretary of State or a person providing services to the Secretary of State or a person engaged in the administration of housing benefit`))
       AND `the information is held only for an excepted purpose`
    THEN TRUE
    ELSE FALSE                                            -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "(a) excepted information is information held by the Welsh body that— (i) is not supplied by ... and (ii) is held only for an excepted purpose"

-- src:2381 | (b) an excepted purpose is a purpose relating to a matter provision for which—
-- src:2382 | (i) is within the legislative competence of the National Assembly for Wales, or
-- src:2383 | (ii) is made by the Welsh Ministers, the First Minister for Wales or the Counsel General to the Welsh Assembly Government.
@ref s 131(7)(b) (src:2381-2383)
GIVEN `the matter is within the legislative competence of the National Assembly for Wales` IS A BOOLEAN  @desc Is provision for the matter within the legislative competence of the National Assembly for Wales?
      `provision for the matter is made by the Welsh Ministers, the First Minister for Wales or the Counsel General` IS A BOOLEAN  @desc Is provision for the matter made by the Welsh Ministers, the First Minister for Wales or the Counsel General to the Welsh Assembly Government?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 131(7)(b) the purpose is an excepted purpose in relation to a Welsh body` MEANS
    IF `the matter is within the legislative competence of the National Assembly for Wales` OR `provision for the matter is made by the Welsh Ministers, the First Minister for Wales or the Counsel General`
    THEN TRUE
    ELSE FALSE                                            -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "(b) an excepted purpose is a purpose relating to a matter provision for which (i) is within the legislative competence of the National Assembly for Wales, or (ii) is made by the Welsh Ministers ..."

-- src:2376 | (6) The Secretary of State may not exercise the power in subsection (3) to prescribe purposes for which information may be supplied by a qualifying person so as to prescribe an excepted purpose in relation to excepted information held by a Welsh body.
@ref s 131(6) (src:2376-2376)
GIVEN `the purpose is an excepted purpose` IS A BOOLEAN  @desc Is the purpose an excepted purpose in relation to a Welsh body?
      `the information is excepted information held by a Welsh body` IS A BOOLEAN  @desc Is the information excepted information held by a Welsh body?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 131(6) regulations may prescribe the purpose for information held by a Welsh body` MEANS
    IF `the purpose is an excepted purpose` AND `the information is excepted information held by a Welsh body`
    THEN JUST FALSE                                       -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The Secretary of State may not exercise the power in subsection (3) to prescribe purposes ... so as to prescribe an excepted purpose in relation to excepted information held by a Welsh body"
    ELSE NOTHING                                          -- NOTHING-kind (limited by own wording): the subsection bars one case; for any other it says nothing

-- src:2386 | (a) excepted information is information held by the Scottish body that—
-- src:2387 | (i) is not supplied by, or derived from information supplied to another person by, the Secretary of State or a person providing services to the Secretary of State or a person engaged in the administration of housing benefit, and
-- src:2388 | (ii) is held only for an excepted purpose;
@ref s 131(9)(a) (src:2386-2388)
GIVEN `the information is supplied by, or derived from information supplied to another person by, the Secretary of State or a person providing services to the Secretary of State or a person engaged in the administration of housing benefit` IS A BOOLEAN  @desc Was the information supplied by, or derived from information supplied by, the Secretary of State, a person providing services to the Secretary of State or a person who administers housing benefit?
      `the information is held only for an excepted purpose` IS A BOOLEAN  @desc Is the information held only for an excepted purpose?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 131(9)(a) the information held by the Scottish body is excepted information` MEANS
    IF (NOT (`the information is supplied by, or derived from information supplied to another person by, the Secretary of State or a person providing services to the Secretary of State or a person engaged in the administration of housing benefit`))
       AND `the information is held only for an excepted purpose`
    THEN TRUE
    ELSE FALSE                                            -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "(a) excepted information is information held by the Scottish body that— (i) is not supplied by ... and (ii) is held only for an excepted purpose"

-- src:2389 | (b) an excepted purpose is a purpose relating to a matter provision for which is within the legislative competence of the Scottish Parliament.
@ref s 131(9)(b) (src:2389-2389)
GIVEN `the matter is within the legislative competence of the Scottish Parliament` IS A BOOLEAN  @desc Is provision for the matter within the legislative competence of the Scottish Parliament?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 131(9)(b) the purpose is an excepted purpose in relation to a Scottish body` MEANS
    IF `the matter is within the legislative competence of the Scottish Parliament`
    THEN TRUE
    ELSE FALSE                                            -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "(b) an excepted purpose is a purpose relating to a matter provision for which is within the legislative competence of the Scottish Parliament"

-- src:2384 | (8) The Secretary of State may not exercise the power in subsection (3) to prescribe purposes for which information may be supplied by a qualifying person so as to prescribe an excepted purpose in relation to excepted information held by a Scottish body.
@ref s 131(8) (src:2384-2384)
GIVEN `the purpose is an excepted purpose` IS A BOOLEAN  @desc Is the purpose an excepted purpose in relation to a Scottish body?
      `the information is excepted information held by a Scottish body` IS A BOOLEAN  @desc Is the information excepted information held by a Scottish body?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 131(8) regulations may prescribe the purpose for information held by a Scottish body` MEANS
    IF `the purpose is an excepted purpose` AND `the information is excepted information held by a Scottish body`
    THEN JUST FALSE                                       -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The Secretary of State may not exercise the power in subsection (3) to prescribe purposes ... so as to prescribe an excepted purpose in relation to excepted information held by a Scottish body"
    ELSE NOTHING                                          -- NOTHING-kind (limited by own wording): the subsection bars one case; for any other it says nothing

-- 131(10): subsections (1) to (4) do not apply in a case where the supply or use is authorised by section 130.
-- src:2390 | (10) Subsections (1) to (4) do not apply in a case where the supply or use of information is authorised by section 130.
@ref s 131(10) (src:2390-2390)
GIVEN `the supply or use of the information is authorised by section 130` IS A BOOLEAN  @desc Is the supply or use of the information authorised by section 130 (overnight care and similar services)?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 131(10) subsections (1) to (4) do not apply` MEANS
    IF `the supply or use of the information is authorised by section 130`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING                                          -- NOTHING-kind (limited by own wording): "do not apply in a case where the supply or use ... is authorised by section 130"; otherwise the subsection is silent

-- 131(12): the defined terms. Where the text says "includes" the list is not closed (NOTHING); where it says "means" it is (FALSE).
-- src:2400 | “council tax” includes any local tax to fund local authority expenditure;
@ref s 131(12) “council tax” (src:2400-2400)
GIVEN `it is council tax` IS A BOOLEAN  @desc Is it council tax?
      `it is a local tax to fund local authority expenditure` IS A BOOLEAN  @desc Is it a local tax to fund local authority expenditure?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 131(12) the tax is council tax` MEANS
    IF `it is council tax` OR `it is a local tax to fund local authority expenditure`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING                                          -- NOTHING-kind (includes): "“council tax” includes any local tax to fund local authority expenditure"

DECLARE `s 131(12) person engaged in the administration of housing benefit` IS ONE OF
    `s 131(12) an authority which administers housing benefit`
    `s 131(12) a person authorised to exercise any function of such an authority relating to housing benefit`
    `s 131(12) a person providing to such an authority services relating to housing benefit`
    `s 131(12) some other person`

-- src:2401 | “person engaged in the administration of housing benefit” means—
-- src:2402 | an authority which administers housing benefit,
-- src:2403 | a person authorised to exercise any function of such an authority relating to housing benefit, or
-- src:2404 | a person providing to such an authority services relating to housing benefit;
@ref s 131(12) “person engaged in the administration of housing benefit” (src:2401-2404)
GIVEN `the person` IS A `s 131(12) person engaged in the administration of housing benefit`  @desc Which description fits the person?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 131(12) the person is engaged in the administration of housing benefit` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the person`
    WHEN `s 131(12) an authority which administers housing benefit` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `s 131(12) a person authorised to exercise any function of such an authority relating to housing benefit` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `s 131(12) a person providing to such an authority services relating to housing benefit` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `s 131(12) some other person` THEN FALSE         -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "“person engaged in the administration of housing benefit” means— an authority ..., a person authorised ..., or a person providing ..."

-- src:2405 | “relevant information” means information relating to—
-- src:2406 | any relevant social security benefit, or
-- src:2407 | welfare services;
@ref s 131(12) “relevant information” (src:2405-2407)
GIVEN `the information relates to a relevant social security benefit` IS A BOOLEAN  @desc Does the information relate to a relevant social security benefit?
      `the information relates to welfare services` IS A BOOLEAN  @desc Does the information relate to welfare services?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 131(12) the information is relevant information` MEANS
    IF `the information relates to a relevant social security benefit` OR `the information relates to welfare services`
    THEN TRUE
    ELSE FALSE                                            -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "“relevant information” means information relating to— any relevant social security benefit, or welfare services"

-- src:2408 | “relevant social security benefit” means—
-- src:2409 | a relevant social security benefit as defined in section 121DA(7) of the Social Security Administration Act 1992, or
-- src:2410 | a loan under section 18 of the Welfare Reform and Work Act 2016 (loans for mortgage interest etc);
@ref s 131(12) “relevant social security benefit” (src:2408-2410)
GIVEN `it is a relevant social security benefit as defined in SSAA section 121DA(7)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN  @desc Is it a relevant social security benefit as defined in section 121DA(7) of the Administration Act? Leave out if not known.
      `it is a loan under section 18 of the Welfare Reform and Work Act 2016` IS A BOOLEAN  @desc Is it a loan under section 18 of the Welfare Reform and Work Act 2016 (loans for mortgage interest)?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 131(12) it is a relevant social security benefit` MEANS
    IF `it is a loan under section 18 of the Welfare Reform and Work Act 2016`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE `it is a relevant social security benefit as defined in SSAA section 121DA(7)`   -- NOTHING-kind (undefined term): "a relevant social security benefit as defined in section 121DA(7)", which is not among the sources

DECLARE `s 131(12) description of a Scottish body` IS ONE OF
    `s 131(12) a local authority in Scotland`
    `s 131(12) a person authorised to exercise any function of a local authority in Scotland relating to welfare services`
    `s 131(12) a person providing to a local authority in Scotland services relating to welfare services`
    `s 131(12) a person prescribed or of a description prescribed by the Secretary of State as a Scottish body`
    `s 131(12) some other person in Scotland`

-- src:2411 | “Scottish body” means—
-- src:2412 | a local authority in Scotland,
-- src:2413 | a person authorised to exercise any function of such an authority relating to welfare services,
-- src:2414 | a person providing to a local authority in Scotland services relating to welfare services, or
-- src:2415 | a person prescribed or of a description prescribed by the Secretary of State;
@ref s 131(12) “Scottish body” (src:2411-2415)
GIVEN `the person` IS A `s 131(12) description of a Scottish body`  @desc Which description fits the person?
      `the Secretary of State prescribes the person` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN  @desc Does the Secretary of State prescribe the person, or a description that fits them, as a Scottish body? Leave out if not known.
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 131(12) the person is a Scottish body` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the person`
    WHEN `s 131(12) a local authority in Scotland` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 131(12) a person authorised to exercise any function of a local authority in Scotland relating to welfare services` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 131(12) a person providing to a local authority in Scotland services relating to welfare services` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 131(12) a person prescribed or of a description prescribed by the Secretary of State as a Scottish body` THEN
        CONSIDER `the Secretary of State prescribes the person`
        WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING                         -- NOTHING-kind (undefined term): who is prescribed is whatever the Secretary of State prescribes
        WHEN JUST prescribed THEN JUST prescribed         -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words) where false: "a person prescribed or of a description prescribed by the Secretary of State"
    WHEN `s 131(12) some other person in Scotland` THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "“Scottish body” means— a local authority in Scotland, ..."

-- src:2416 | “welfare services” includes services which provide accommodation, support, assistance, advice or counselling to individuals with particular needs, and for these purposes “assistance” includes assistance by means of a grant or loan or the provision of goods or services;
@ref s 131(12) “welfare services” (src:2416-2416)
GIVEN `it provides accommodation, support, assistance, advice or counselling to individuals with particular needs` IS A BOOLEAN  @desc Does the service provide accommodation, support, assistance (including a grant, a loan, goods or services), advice or counselling to individuals with particular needs?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 131(12) the service is welfare services` MEANS
    IF `it provides accommodation, support, assistance, advice or counselling to individuals with particular needs`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING                                          -- NOTHING-kind (includes): "“welfare services” includes services which provide accommodation, support, assistance, advice or counselling to individuals with particular needs"

DECLARE `s 131(12) description of a Welsh body` IS ONE OF
    `s 131(12) a local authority in Wales`
    `s 131(12) a person authorised to exercise any function of a local authority in Wales relating to welfare services`
    `s 131(12) a person providing to a local authority in Wales services relating to welfare services`
    `s 131(12) a person prescribed or of a description prescribed by the Secretary of State as a Welsh body`
    `s 131(12) some other person in Wales`

-- src:2417 | “Welsh body” means—
-- src:2418 | a local authority in Wales,
-- src:2419 | a person authorised to exercise any function of such an authority relating to welfare services,
-- src:2420 | a person providing to a local authority in Wales services relating to welfare services, or
-- src:2421 | a person prescribed or of a description prescribed by the Secretary of State.
@ref s 131(12) “Welsh body” (src:2417-2421)
GIVEN `the person` IS A `s 131(12) description of a Welsh body`  @desc Which description fits the person?
      `the Secretary of State prescribes the person` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN  @desc Does the Secretary of State prescribe the person, or a description that fits them, as a Welsh body? Leave out if not known.
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 131(12) the person is a Welsh body` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the person`
    WHEN `s 131(12) a local authority in Wales` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 131(12) a person authorised to exercise any function of a local authority in Wales relating to welfare services` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 131(12) a person providing to a local authority in Wales services relating to welfare services` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 131(12) a person prescribed or of a description prescribed by the Secretary of State as a Welsh body` THEN
        CONSIDER `the Secretary of State prescribes the person`
        WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING                         -- NOTHING-kind (undefined term): who is prescribed is whatever the Secretary of State prescribes
        WHEN JUST prescribed THEN JUST prescribed         -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words) where false: "a person prescribed or of a description prescribed by the Secretary of State"
    WHEN `s 131(12) some other person in Wales` THEN JUST FALSE      -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "“Welsh body” means— a local authority in Wales, ..."

§ `s 132 -- unlawful disclosure of information supplied under section 131`

-- 132(2): subsection (2) applies to (a) a person mentioned in section 131(11)(a) to (c), (b) a person who provides qualifying
-- welfare services, (c) a person who is or has been a director, member of the committee of management, manager, secretary or
-- other similar officer of a person in (a) or (b), (d) a person who is or has been an employee of a person in (a) or (b).
DECLARE `s 132(2) description of person` IS ONE OF
    `s 132(2)(a) a person mentioned in section 131(11)(a) to (c)`
    `s 132(2)(b) a person who provides qualifying welfare services within the meaning of section 131`
    `s 132(2)(c) a person who is or has been a director, member of the committee of management, manager, secretary or other similar officer of a person mentioned in paragraph (a) or (b)`
    `s 132(2)(d) a person who is or has been an employee of a person mentioned in paragraph (a) or (b)`
    `s 132(2) some other person`

-- src:2426 | (2) This subsection applies to—
-- src:2427 | (a) a person mentioned in section 131(11) (a) to (c);
-- src:2428 | (b) a person who provides qualifying welfare services (within the meaning of section 131);
-- src:2429 | (c) a person who is or has been a director, member of the committee of management, manager, secretary or other similar officer of a person mentioned in paragraph (a) or (b);
-- src:2430 | (d) a person who is or has been an employee of a person mentioned in paragraph (a) or (b).
@ref s 132(2) (src:2426-2430)
GIVEN `the person` IS A `s 132(2) description of person`  @desc Which description fits the person?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 132(2) subsection (2) applies to the person` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the person`
    WHEN `s 132(2)(a) a person mentioned in section 131(11)(a) to (c)` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `s 132(2)(b) a person who provides qualifying welfare services within the meaning of section 131` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `s 132(2)(c) a person who is or has been a director, member of the committee of management, manager, secretary or other similar officer of a person mentioned in paragraph (a) or (b)` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `s 132(2)(d) a person who is or has been an employee of a person mentioned in paragraph (a) or (b)` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `s 132(2) some other person` THEN FALSE           -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "This subsection applies to (a) ... (b) ... (c) ... (d) ..."

-- 132(1): a person to whom subsection (2) applies is guilty of an offence if the person discloses without lawful authority any
-- information (a) which comes to the person by virtue of section 131(1), (3) or (4), and (b) which relates to a particular person.
-- src:2423 | (1) A person to whom subsection (2) applies is guilty of an offence if the person discloses without lawful authority any information—
-- src:2424 | (a) which comes to the person by virtue of section 131(1), (3) or (4), and
-- src:2425 | (b) which relates to a particular person.
@ref s 132(1) (src:2423-2425)
GIVEN `subsection (2) applies to the person` IS A BOOLEAN  @desc Does one of the descriptions in section 132(2) fit you?
      `the person discloses the information without lawful authority` IS A BOOLEAN  @desc Do you disclose the information without lawful authority?
      `the information comes to the person by virtue of section 131(1), (3) or (4)` IS A BOOLEAN  @desc Did the information come to you by virtue of section 131(1), (3) or (4)?
      `the information relates to a particular person` IS A BOOLEAN  @desc Does the information relate to a particular person?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 132(1) the person is guilty of an offence` MEANS
    IF `subsection (2) applies to the person` AND `the person discloses the information without lawful authority`
       AND `the information comes to the person by virtue of section 131(1), (3) or (4)` AND `the information relates to a particular person`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING                                          -- NOTHING-kind (limited by own wording): "is guilty of an offence if" these four things; the subsection says nothing of any other case

-- 132(3): the same penalties as section 129(7); 132(9): the same reading of the general limit before 2 May 2022 as 129(9).
-- src:2431 | (3) A person guilty of an offence under this section is liable—
-- src:2432 | (a) on conviction on indictment, to imprisonment for a term not exceeding two years or a fine or both, or
-- src:2433 | (b) on summary conviction, to imprisonment for a term not exceeding the general limit in a magistrates’ court or a fine not exceeding the statutory maximum or both.
@ref s 132(3) (src:2431-2433)
GIVEN `the mode of conviction` IS A `s 129(7) mode of conviction`  @desc Would you be convicted on indictment or summarily?
GIVETH A `s 129(7) punishment`
`s 132(3) the greatest punishment for the offence` MEANS
    `s 129(7) the greatest punishment for the offence` `the mode of conviction`

-- src:2445 | (9) In relation to an offence under this section committed in England and Wales before 2 May 2022 the reference in subsection (3) (b) to the general limit in a magistrates’ court must be taken to be a reference to six months.
@ref s 132(9) (src:2445-2445)
GIVEN `the term` IS A `s 129(7) term of imprisonment`  @desc Which term applies to you?
      `the offence was committed in England and Wales before 2 May 2022` IS A BOOLEAN  @desc Was the offence committed in England and Wales before 2 May 2022?
GIVETH A `s 129(7) term of imprisonment`
`s 132(9) the term as read for an offence committed before 2 May 2022` MEANS
    `s 129(9) the term as read for an offence committed before 2 May 2022` `the term` `the offence was committed in England and Wales before 2 May 2022`

-- 132(4): it is not an offence under the section (a) to disclose information in a form that does not enable information about a
-- particular person to be ascertained, or (b) to disclose information previously disclosed to the public with lawful authority.
-- src:2434 | (4) It is not an offence under this section—
-- src:2435 | (a) to disclose information in the form of a summary or collection of information so framed as not to enable information relating to any particular person to be ascertained from it;
-- src:2436 | (b) to disclose information which has previously been disclosed to the public with lawful authority.
@ref s 132(4) (src:2434-2436)
GIVEN `the disclosure is of a summary or collection of information so framed as not to enable information relating to any particular person to be ascertained from it` IS A BOOLEAN  @desc Is the disclosure a summary or collection of information that does not enable information about any particular person to be ascertained?
      `the information has previously been disclosed to the public with lawful authority` IS A BOOLEAN  @desc Has the information previously been disclosed to the public with lawful authority?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 132(4) the disclosure is not an offence under this section` MEANS
    IF `the disclosure is of a summary or collection of information so framed as not to enable information relating to any particular person to be ascertained from it`
       OR `the information has previously been disclosed to the public with lawful authority`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING                                          -- NOTHING-kind (limited by own wording): "It is not an offence ... (a) ... (b) ..."; for any other disclosure the subsection is silent

-- 132(5): a defence for D charged with an offence under the section, who proves that at the time D (a) believed that D was
-- making the disclosure with lawful authority and had no reasonable cause to believe otherwise, or (b) believed that the
-- information had previously been disclosed to the public with lawful authority and had no reasonable cause to believe otherwise.
-- src:2437 | (5) It is a defence for a person (“D”) charged with an offence under this section to prove that at the time of the alleged offence—
-- src:2438 | (a) D believed that D was making the disclosure in question with lawful authority and had no reasonable cause to believe otherwise, or
-- src:2439 | (b) D believed that the information in question had previously been disclosed to the public with lawful authority and had no reasonable cause to believe otherwise.
@ref s 132(5) (src:2437-2439)
GIVEN `the person is charged with an offence under this section` IS A BOOLEAN  @desc Are you charged with an offence under section 132?
      `the person proves that they believed they were making the disclosure with lawful authority and had no reasonable cause to believe otherwise` IS A BOOLEAN  @desc Can you prove that you believed you were making the disclosure with lawful authority and had no reasonable cause to believe otherwise?
      `the person proves that they believed the information had previously been disclosed to the public with lawful authority and had no reasonable cause to believe otherwise` IS A BOOLEAN  @desc Can you prove that you believed the information had previously been disclosed to the public with lawful authority and had no reasonable cause to believe otherwise?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 132(5) the person has a defence` MEANS
    IF `the person is charged with an offence under this section`
       AND (`the person proves that they believed they were making the disclosure with lawful authority and had no reasonable cause to believe otherwise`
            OR `the person proves that they believed the information had previously been disclosed to the public with lawful authority and had no reasonable cause to believe otherwise`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING                                          -- NOTHING-kind (limited by own wording): "It is a defence ... to prove that"; the subsection does not say there is no defence otherwise

-- 132(6): a disclosure is made with lawful authority if it is so made for the purposes of section 123 of the Social Security
-- Administration Act 1992.
-- src:2440 | (6) A disclosure is made with lawful authority if it is so made for the purposes of section 123 of the Social Security Administration Act 1992.
@ref s 132(6) (src:2440-2440)
GIVEN `the disclosure is made for the purposes of section 123 of the Social Security Administration Act 1992` IS A BOOLEAN  @desc Is the disclosure made for the purposes of section 123 of the Social Security Administration Act 1992?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 132(6) the disclosure is made with lawful authority` MEANS
    IF `the disclosure is made for the purposes of section 123 of the Social Security Administration Act 1992`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING                                          -- NOTHING-kind (limited by own wording): "A disclosure is made with lawful authority if it is so made for the purposes of section 123"; other sources of lawful authority are not excluded

§ `s 133 -- sections 130 to 132: supplementary`

-- 133(1): "benefit" includes any allowance, payment, credit or loan.
-- src:2448 | “benefit” includes any allowance, payment, credit or loan;
@ref s 133(1) “benefit” (src:2448-2448)
GIVEN `it is an allowance, payment, credit or loan` IS A BOOLEAN  @desc Is it an allowance, payment, credit or loan?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 133(1) the thing is a benefit` MEANS
    IF `it is an allowance, payment, credit or loan`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING                                          -- NOTHING-kind (includes): "“benefit” includes any allowance, payment, credit or loan"

-- 133(1): "local authority" means one of seven kinds of council. A closed definition.
DECLARE `s 133(1) kind of council` IS ONE OF
    `s 133(1) a county or district council in England`
    `s 133(1) an eligible parish council within the meaning of Chapter 1 of Part 1 of the Localism Act 2011`
    `s 133(1) a London borough council`
    `s 133(1) the Common Council of the City of London in its capacity as a local authority`
    `s 133(1) the Council of the Isles of Scilly`
    `s 133(1) a county or county borough council in Wales`
    `s 133(1) a council constituted under section 2 of the Local Government etc. (Scotland) Act 1994`
    `s 133(1) some other body`

-- src:2449 | “local authority” means—
-- src:2450 | a county or district council in England;
-- src:2451 | an eligible parish council (within the meaning of Chapter 1 of Part 1 of the Localism Act 2011);
-- src:2452 | a London borough council;
-- src:2453 | the Common Council of the City of London in its capacity as a local authority;
-- src:2454 | the Council of the Isles of Scilly;
-- src:2455 | a county or county borough council in Wales;
-- src:2456 | a council constituted under section 2 of the Local Government etc. (Scotland) Act 1994;
@ref s 133(1) “local authority” (src:2449-2456)
GIVEN `the body` IS A `s 133(1) kind of council`  @desc What kind of body is it?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 133(1) the body is a local authority` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the body`
    WHEN `s 133(1) a county or district council in England` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `s 133(1) an eligible parish council within the meaning of Chapter 1 of Part 1 of the Localism Act 2011` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `s 133(1) a London borough council` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `s 133(1) the Common Council of the City of London in its capacity as a local authority` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `s 133(1) the Council of the Isles of Scilly` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `s 133(1) a county or county borough council in Wales` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `s 133(1) a council constituted under section 2 of the Local Government etc. (Scotland) Act 1994` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `s 133(1) some other body` THEN FALSE            -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "“local authority” means— a county or district council in England; ... ; a council constituted under section 2 of the Local Government etc. (Scotland) Act 1994"

-- 133(1): "prescribed" means prescribed in regulations made by the Secretary of State: the same as the definition in section 96(10).
-- src:2457 | “prescribed” means prescribed in regulations made by the Secretary of State.
@ref s 133(1) “prescribed” (src:2457-2457)
GIVEN `the matter is set out in regulations` IS A BOOLEAN  @desc Is the matter set out in regulations?
      `the maker of the regulations` IS AN Authority  @desc Who made the regulations?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 133(1) the matter is prescribed` MEANS
    `s 96(10) the matter is prescribed` `the matter is set out in regulations` `the maker of the regulations`

-- 133(5): until the provision for identifying eligible parish councils under Chapter 1 of Part 1 of the Localism Act 2011 comes
-- into force, the reference in (1) is read as a reference to an eligible parish council within the meaning of Part 1 of the
-- Local Government Act 2000.
DECLARE `s 133(5) Act that gives the meaning of eligible parish council` IS ONE OF
    `s 133(1) Chapter 1 of Part 1 of the Localism Act 2011`
    `s 133(5) Part 1 of the Local Government Act 2000`

-- src:2463 | (5) Until the coming into force of provision for identifying eligible parish councils within the meaning of Chapter 1 of Part 1 of the Localism Act 2011, the reference in subsection (1) to an eligible parish council within the meaning of that Chapter is to be read as a reference to an eligible parish council within the meaning of Part 1 of the Local Government Act 2000.
@ref s 133(5) (src:2463-2463)
GIVEN `the provision for identifying eligible parish councils under Chapter 1 of Part 1 of the Localism Act 2011 has come into force` IS A BOOLEAN  @desc Has the provision for identifying eligible parish councils under Chapter 1 of Part 1 of the Localism Act 2011 come into force?
GIVETH A `s 133(5) Act that gives the meaning of eligible parish council`
`s 133(5) the Act that gives the meaning of eligible parish council` MEANS
    IF `the provision for identifying eligible parish councils under Chapter 1 of Part 1 of the Localism Act 2011 has come into force`
    THEN `s 133(1) Chapter 1 of Part 1 of the Localism Act 2011`
    ELSE `s 133(5) Part 1 of the Local Government Act 2000`
